# Store every text file as LF in the index, on every platform.
#
# Why this exists: the chat page was dead in production because its inline
# bootstrap was pinned by a SHA-256 CSP hash. Windows checked the file out with
# CRLF while the tooling that computed the hash read LF bytes, so the hash
# silently drifted from the served content and the browser blocked the whole
# app. Normalising the index to LF removes the line-ending churn that made the
# served bytes differ from the reviewed bytes; the drift-guard test
# (test/no_inline_scripts.test.ts) covers the CSP side of the same failure.
* text=auto eol=lf
